Aura downstream FEX IR block-tail maintenance optimization

Based on FEX-Emu/FEX revision 14c92681f4d62cf84d901460e0358de09c8847a7
(FEX-2610), MIT. https://github.com/FEX-Emu/FEX

This Aura downstream change is not an upstream contribution. It caches the tail
of the current emitter's linked code-block list, updates it on tail insertion,
and invalidates it on reset, copy and tail removal. It retains block ordering,
instruction checks, invalidation exits, guest memory accesses and cache policy.
No game code, game resources or user diagnostics are included.

The host differential tests compile the actual before/after IREmitter and compare
synthetic IR output. Host timings are not Android frame-rate measurements.
